Privacy Policy for Smart Home
Last Updated: February 12, 2025

1. Introduction
Thank you for using Smart Home. Your privacy is important to us, and this policy outlines how we collect, use, and protect your data.

2. Information Collected
Smart Home collects and stores the following information locally on your device:

Device Credentials: BLID, password, and IP address for connecting to smart home devices (e.g., Roomba).
User Preferences: Theme settings and customization options.
3. How We Use Your Data
Your data is used solely for connecting and controlling your smart home devices.
No information is transmitted externally or shared with third parties.
4. Data Security
The app does not collect or send personal data to any servers.
Your credentials are stored locally on your device and are not shared externally.
5. Your Choices
You can modify or delete your credentials anytime through the app settings.
Uninstalling the app removes all stored data from your device.
6. Third-Party Services
Smart Home does not integrate with third-party analytics, tracking, or cloud services.

7. Changes to This Policy
We may update this privacy policy if necessary. Any changes will be reflected here and within the app.
